    "result_text": "I added `mailserver()` to `CTFd/utils/config/__init__.py`, just above `mailgun()`. I haven't run any tests.\n\nIt returns `True` if `MAIL_SERVER` and `MAIL_PORT` are both set in the app config, or if the admin settings `mail_server` and `mail_port` are both set. Otherwise it returns `False`. That matches how `get_mail_provider()` in the same file decides SMTP is configured.\n\n`can_send_mail()` in that file already called `mailserver()`, but it wasn't defined anywhere, so that call would have raised a `NameError`. It should work now.\n\nI built it from the catalog pattern `config.mail_provider_configured@v1`, which is the `mailgun()` check, and swapped in the SMTP keys. The marker comment stays above the function. The `check_code` run on the file's real imports reports only low-severity \"literal changed\" notes for the SMTP keys, and no high-severity deviations, so no `pcat-allow` approval is needed.\n\nMy first `check_code` run flagged a high-severity \"library swapped\" deviation. That was because I'd passed only the function body, without its `flask` and `get_config` imports. It disappeared once I included them."
